{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And any uncircumcised male who shall not be circumcised.</b> The meaning: ימול is reflexive-active [יפעול], like \"ידור נדר\" (Numbers 30:3), and it is from \"ונמלתם את בשר ערלתכם\" (Genesis 17:11). Its sense: if he was of mitzvah age and did not circumcise the flesh of his foreskin, there is upon him karet, for the commandment of the minor child is upon the father. And if his father did not circumcise him, he must circumcise himself when he is in his own jurisdiction, and karet is by the hand of Heaven. And the erring ones will reckon, for if the child died and was not circumcised, he has no share in the world to come — but the meaning of נפש is not as they wish, for נפש is like איש, meaning a body that has a soul, as in \"נפש כי תחטא\" (Leviticus 4:2). Some say that karet of the dead one is before the age of fifty-two; some say that karet means that his name will be cut off by the death of his seed, therefore Scripture says \"מעמיה,\" for one who has children is as though he is alive and his name is not cut off."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "Resolved abbreviation נ\"ב as fifty-two (years), standard Rabbinic halakhic age for karet; resolved הטועים as 'the erring ones' (referring to misinterpreters of the term נפש)."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:55.164326684Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}